1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:07,496
From June 2027, every EU employer with more than one hundred and fifty
staff must publish its gender pay gap.

2
00:00:07,447 --> 00:00:12,643
GotIt produces that report from a ledger that holds counts, and never
a salary.

3
00:00:13,250 --> 00:00:15,752
The directive sets a trap.

4
00:00:15,702 --> 00:00:22,850
You must publish group statistics, and data protection law says those
same statistics must never identify anyone.

5
00:00:22,850 --> 00:00:28,032
Today it is solved by exporting a spreadsheet and deleting small
groups by hand.

6
00:00:28,032 --> 00:00:31,104
That is an assertion nobody can check.

7
00:00:31,719 --> 00:00:35,965
This is the live report, read from a contract on Preprod.

8
00:00:35,915 --> 00:00:38,454
No wallet, no account.

9
00:00:38,454 --> 00:00:41,306
Thirteen people have contributed.

10
00:00:41,306 --> 00:00:49,757
Engineering has five women and five men, and the gap is material, so
the report flags it and the interval shows how far it can be trusted.

11
00:00:50,359 --> 00:00:52,823
Everything else is withheld.

12
00:00:52,772 --> 00:01:04,855
The contract returns zero for any group below the anonymity threshold,
and that gate is evaluated inside the circuit, so the employer who

13
00:01:05,469 --> 00:01:08,505
Anyone can check a published report.

14
00:01:08,454 --> 00:01:14,028
Paste its fingerprint, and the page re-reads chain state and answers
match or mismatch.

15
00:01:14,028 --> 00:01:17,414
No wallet, no account, no permission.

16
00:01:18,019 --> 00:01:21,823
The figures are reproducible, not just asserted.

17
00:01:21,774 --> 00:01:31,709
